      <div class="entity-eyebrow">
        <span class="entity-class">Non-Governmental Entity · Militant · Political Party · Sunni Islamist</span>
        <span class="entity-status-chip status-degraded">⬤ Severely Degraded · Rebuilding</span>
      </div>

      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:4px;">
        <div style="width:52px;height:34px;border:0.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15);border-radius:2px;flex-shrink:0;background:#006233;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;overflow:hidden;">
          <div style="text-align:center;line-height:1.1;">
            <div style="font-size:9px;color:white;font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:0.02em;">حماس</div>
            <div style="font-size:6px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;margin-top:1px;">☽✦</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="entity-endonym">حَرَكَة المُقَاوَمَة الإِسْلَامِيَّة — Ḥarakat al-Muqāwamah al-Islāmīyah</div>
          <div class="entity-name">Hamas</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="entity-aliases">Also: Islamic Resistance Movement · Harakat al-Muqawama al-Islamiya · HAMAS (acronym)</div>

      <div class="entity-summary">
        A Palestinian <span class="term" onclick="showDef('sunni')">Sunni</span> Islamist organization founded in 1987 during the First Intifada as an offshoot of the <span class="term" onclick="showDef('mb')">Egyptian Muslim Brotherhood</span>. Since 2007, Hamas has governed the <span class="term" onclick="showDef('gaza')">Gaza Strip</span> after winning the 2006 Palestinian legislative elections and seizing control from <span class="term" onclick="showDef('fatah')">Fatah</span> in a brief civil conflict. It is simultaneously a political party, a militant organization (<span class="term" onclick="showDef('qassam')">Izz ad-Din al-Qassam Brigades</span>), a social services network, and the de facto government of 2.3 million Palestinians. Funded primarily by <span class="term" onclick="showDef('iran')">Iran</span> (~$100M/year pre-2023) and <span class="term" onclick="showDef('qatar')">Qatar</span> (~$30M/month for civilian administration). Hamas's relationship with Iran is <em>ideologically unusual</em> — it is a Sunni organization sponsored by a Shia state, a pragmatic alliance of shared opposition to Israel rather than theological alignment.
        <br><br>
        On October 7, 2023, Hamas led coordinated attacks into Israel killing 1,200 people and taking 251 hostages — the deadliest day for Jews since the Holocaust. The subsequent Israeli military campaign has killed 70,000+ Palestinians, destroyed Gaza's infrastructure, and decapitated Hamas's military and political leadership. By March 2026 Hamas is severely degraded militarily but its political bureau in Qatar and Turkey remains intact.
