    <div class="tab-section">
      <div class="ts-eyebrow">1987 — 2026</div>
      <div class="ts-title">Hamas: Four Decades</div>
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot active"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">December 1987</div><div class="tl-event">Hamas founded by Sheikh Ahmed Yassin during First Intifada as Muslim Brotherhood offshoot. Explicitly rejects PLO's secular nationalism and Oslo framework.</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">1990s</div><div class="tl-event">Suicide bombing campaign against Israel. Hamas opposes Oslo Accords (1993). Iran becomes primary weapons supplier. US designates as FTO (1997).</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">January 2006</div><div class="tl-event">Hamas wins Palestinian Legislative Council elections with 74 of 132 seats. International community refuses to recognize result unless Hamas recognizes Israel, renounces violence, and accepts prior agreements.</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">June 2007</div><div class="tl-event">Hamas seizes Gaza in brief civil war against Fatah. Palestinian Authority retains West Bank; Hamas controls Gaza. Palestinian territory formally split between two rival governments.</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">2007–2023</div><div class="tl-event">Gaza under blockade by Israel and Egypt. Three major wars (2008–09, 2012, 2014). Hamas builds tunnel network. Iron Dome development accelerated. Qatar begins civilian funding ($30M/month) with Israeli tacit acceptance to prevent Hamas collapse and Gazan humanitarian catastrophe.</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">2012–2017</div><div class="tl-event">Hamas backs Syrian Sunni opposition against Assad. Iran cuts funding. Hamas moves HQ from Damascus to Qatar. Iran shifts support to PIJ as primary Gaza proxy.</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">2022</div><div class="tl-event">Hamas reconciles with Iran. Funding restored. Joint operations coordination resumes.</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot" style="background:#8b1a1a;border-color:#c0392b;"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">October 7, 2023</div><div class="tl-event">Hamas-led attack into Israel: 1,200 killed, 251 taken hostage — deadliest day for Jews since the Holocaust. Planned by Qassam Brigades over 2+ years in operational silence. Iran not briefed in advance (US intelligence assessment).</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot" style="background:#8b1a1a;"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">Oct 2023 – Oct 2025</div><div class="tl-event">IDF Gaza campaign. 70,000+ Palestinian deaths. 85% population displaced. All three top military commanders killed (Deif Aug 2024, Issa Mar 2024, Sinwar Oct 2024). Haniyeh assassinated in Tehran Jul 2024. Gaza infrastructure largely destroyed.</div></div></div>
        <div class="tl-item"><div class="tl-dot active"></div><div class="tl-content"><div class="tl-date">October 2025</div><div class="tl-event">Gaza ceasefire Phase 1 — hostage releases in exchange for Palestinian prisoner releases. Hamas political bureau negotiates from Qatar. Military wing severely degraded but organizationally intact in tunnel network.</div></div></div>
