  <!-- ══ RELATIONSHIPS ══ -->
  <div class="entity-tab-content" id="tab-relationships">
    <div class="tab-section">
      <div class="ts-eyebrow">Network mapping</div>
      <div class="ts-title">Hamas in the Regional Network</div>

      <div class="rel-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;">
        <div class="rel-card">
          <div class="rc-header" style="background:rgba(139,26,26,0.3);">Iran — Primary weapons sponsor</div>
          <div class="rc-body">Provides ~$100M/year pre-2023 (since reduced). Supplies rockets, training, technical expertise for tunnel construction and drone development. Relationship is <strong>transactional not theological</strong> — Iran is Shia, Hamas is Sunni. When Hamas backed Syrian Sunni rebels (2012–17), Iran cut ties and resumed only after reconciliation. US intelligence assesses Iran had no foreknowledge of Oct 7.</div>
          <div class="rc-status" style="color:#FAC775;">⬤ Strained · Supply chain disrupted Feb 2026</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rel-card">
          <div class="rc-header" style="background:rgba(27,58,107,0.4);">Qatar — Civilian funding &amp; political host</div>
          <div class="rc-body">Provides ~$30M/month for Gaza civilian administration (salaries, utilities) with Israeli and US tacit approval as alternative to Hamas collapse. Hosts Hamas political bureau in Doha. Qatar maintains this role because it serves as ceasefire mediator — cannot mediate without direct Hamas contact. Qatar is not an FTO designator of Hamas.</div>
          <div class="rc-status" style="color:#C0DD97;">⬤ Active · Ongoing ceasefire mediation role</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rel-card">
          <div class="rc-header" style="background:rgba(27,58,107,0.4);">Turkey — Political support</div>
          <div class="rc-body">Erdoğan has called Hamas leaders by phone, hosted them in Ankara, and refused to designate Hamas as a terrorist organization. Turkey's position: Hamas represents legitimate Palestinian political resistance elected in 2006. This creates friction with NATO allies but Turkey has maintained the position consistently. Not a weapons supplier.</div>
          <div class="rc-status" style="color:#C0DD97;">⬤ Active · Political and diplomatic</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rel-card">
          <div class="rc-header" style="background:rgba(196,127,0,0.2);">Palestinian Islamic Jihad — Gaza coordination</div>
          <div class="rc-body">PIJ is Hamas's smaller partner in Gaza — more directly Iranian, more doctrinally rigid. Both participated in Oct 7. Iran boosted PIJ funding during 2012–17 Hamas estrangement. PIJ has fewer fighters (~5,000) but operates with more Iranian direction. Relationship is cooperative-competitive: both share Gaza and anti-Israel objectives but compete for funding and influence.</div>
          <div class="rc-status" style="color:#FAC775;">⬤ Coordinated · Also severely degraded</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rel-card">
          <div class="rc-header" style="background:rgba(80,19,19,0.3);">Israel — Active conflict relationship</div>
          <div class="rc-body">Hamas does not recognize Israel's right to exist. Its founding charter called for Israel's destruction (revised 2017 charter softened this slightly). Israel designates Hamas as a terrorist organization and has conducted multiple military campaigns against it. Israel simultaneously allowed Qatar funding because Hamas governance was preferred to chaos. Oct 7 ended this calculation.</div>
          <div class="rc-status" style="color:#ffaaaa;">⬤ Active conflict · Phase 1 ceasefire holding</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rel-card">
          <div class="rc-header" style="background:rgba(80,19,19,0.3);">Palestinian Authority / Fatah — Rival Palestinian authority</div>
          <div class="rc-body">PA controls West Bank; Hamas controls Gaza. They are rival governments of the same claimed territory. Multiple reconciliation attempts have failed. PA has cooperated with Israeli security coordination — Hamas calls this collaboration. Hamas sees the PA as a collaborationist authority; the PA sees Hamas as an illegitimate coup government. No unified Palestinian leadership since 2007.</div>
          <div class="rc-status" style="color:#ffaaaa;">⬤ Hostile · No reconciliation</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

