      <div class="ts-title">Terrorist Designation — A Split World</div>
      <div class="ts-body" style="margin-bottom:20px;">Hamas's designation status is uniquely divided — more so than almost any other organization. The Western bloc, Israel, and some others designate it as a terrorist organization. Qatar, Turkey, Russia, China, and much of the Global South do not. This split is not merely diplomatic — it reflects a genuine disagreement about whether Hamas represents terrorism or legitimate armed resistance to occupation. FORA records all positions.</div>
