          <tr><td>China</td><td style="color:#C0DD97;font-weight:700;">Not designated</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>China has hosted Hamas delegations and calls for Palestinian unity government.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>UN</td><td style="color:#FAC775;font-weight:700;">Not designated</td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td>No UN Security Council designation — Russia and China would veto. Hamas is not on the UN Consolidated Sanctions List.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jordan</td><td style="color:#ffaaaa;font-weight:700;">Designated / banned</td><td>Hamas political activity banned in Jordan</td><td>1999 (banned)</td><td>Jordan expelled Hamas leadership in 1999. Relations partially normalized but Hamas activities remain restricted.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Egypt</td><td style="color:#FAC775;font-weight:700;">Complex</td><td>Court designations reversed; ambiguous status</td><td>Varies</td><td>Egyptian courts have designated and de-designated Hamas. Government maintains working relationship with Hamas for Gaza border management while restricting its activities.</td></tr>
