      <div class="ci-list">
        <div class="ci-card"><div class="ci-icon">⚖️</div><div><div class="ci-title">Is Hamas a terrorist organization or a legitimate resistance movement?</div><div class="ci-desc">The designation question is not merely legal — it reflects fundamentally different frameworks for understanding political violence, occupation, and self-determination. Western law, Islamic law, and international law give different answers.</div><div class="ci-count">3,847 contributions · 42 jurisdictions</div></div><div class="ci-arrow">→</div></div>
        <div class="ci-card"><div class="ci-icon">🗳️</div><div><div class="ci-title">Does Hamas's 2006 electoral mandate confer legitimacy to its governance?</div><div class="ci-desc">Hamas won the only free Palestinian election. It then seized Gaza by force. The international community refused to recognize the result. The PA has not held elections since. What does democratic legitimacy require?</div><div class="ci-count">1,204 contributions · 18 jurisdictions</div></div><div class="ci-arrow">→</div></div>
        <div class="ci-card"><div class="ci-icon">🧩</div><div><div class="ci-title">Can Hamas be negotiated with toward a two-state solution?</div><div class="ci-desc">Hamas's founding charter rejected Israel's existence. The 2017 revised charter softened but did not eliminate this. Some analysts argue engagement is necessary; others that Hamas's acceptance of a Palestinian state alongside Israel is incompatible with its ideology.</div><div class="ci-count">2,109 contributions · 31 jurisdictions</div></div><div class="ci-arrow">→</div></div>
        <div class="ci-card"><div class="ci-icon">📊</div><div><div class="ci-title">How should Oct 7 be framed — terrorism, war crime, act of resistance, or all three?</div><div class="ci-desc">The attack killed civilians, took hostages, and was meticulously planned. International law, Israeli law, Palestinian law, and Islamic law each provide different analytical frameworks. Multiple framings can be simultaneously true under different legal systems.</div><div class="ci-count">5,621 contributions · 67 jurisdictions · Highest-traffic CivicIssue</div></div><div class="ci-arrow">→</div></div>
